{
  "kind": "run8",
  "comment": "Pose guides for the 8-direction, 8-frame run sheet; conventions as walk8.json. A run is not a fast walk: the stride is half again as long, the body bob is twice as deep, the torso leans forward over the hips, the elbows are bent hard so the hands swing at chest height rather than by the thigh, and frames 3 and 7 are flight -- both feet off the ground -- which is the thing that separates the two gaits at a glance. The trailing leg tucks its heel towards the hip on the recovery instead of swinging through straight. The front and back rows keep walk8's rule and carry the cycle in the bob and the lifted feet.",
